@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+R1 (B1, B10) Queue (programmatic) wake is enabled per seat; the node-level programmatic_wake setting has no effect after upgrade (no migration onto seats) and an existing node file with it still loads.
+R2 (B2) A generic per-seat key=value config exists, stored and decided by the daemon, with a typed registry of supported keys (description, values, default, write tier).
+R3 (B3, B6) Every caller, including non-human and subagents, can read any seat's config values.
+R4 (B4, B5) A command lists every supported per-seat key with what it does, its possible values, default and write tier, so an agent told in prose can find and set the right key with the right command.
+R5 (B6, B7) Agent-tier keys, including nudge threshold, are writable through the non-human path on the caller's own seat.
+R6 (B6, B10) Human-tier keys (programmatic_wake) are writable only through `ht human config seat set`, which may target any local seat; the agent path refuses them and names the human command.
+R7 (B7, B10) nudge_threshold is a key over the existing seat column; nudge-threshold and wake-on keep working unchanged.
+R8 (B8) With a used /side chat in the same Codex process, an owed idle wake reaches the root session through the queue by exact session UUID, never the side session.
+R9 (B8) Live spikes establish root vs side identity, concurrency, arrival identity and UI effects, and their answers drive the routing rules.
+R10 (B9) Native wake never types into a displayed /side chat; it defers.
+R11 (B8, B10) The new routing and per-seat enablement are qualified live (side-queue/group and existing queue-proof cases) and release tooling enables queue wake per seat.
+R12 TRUST-POLICY records the seat-config write rules and the accepted limit of the human tier in the same commit as the code.
+R13 (R-new, both reviewers; B6) The harness permission ask-rules setup installs cover `ht human config seat set` and `herdr-threads human config seat set`.
+R14 (R-new, both reviewers) A CLI against a daemon without seat.config_v1 is refused with a stated one-line message.
+R15 (R-new, both reviewers; B1) User docs and CHANGELOG describe the per-seat key and that node programmatic_wake no longer takes effect.
+R16 (R-new, reviewer B; B9) Native defer on a displayed /side chat with queue off is qualified live.
